Translation patch: `Option`/`Result` combinators in `value::convert::{chrono, time}`

Change: `if let Some((date, time)) = date.zip(time)` becomes `if let (Some(date), Some(time)) = (date, time)`; `str_from_utf8(b).ok_or_else(|| e).and_then(|s| ..)` becomes `match str_from_utf8(b) { None => Err(e), Some(s) => .. }`; and in `TryFrom<Value> for ParseIr<Date>`, `match str_from_utf8(b).and_then(|s| parse(s)) { .. }` becomes nested `match`es.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Option::zip`, `Option::ok_or_else`, `Result::and_then` and `Option::and_then`; and it fails ("Internal error") on a `match` whose result is matched again while `v` is borrowed by `ref bytes`, so the matches are nested in tail position.
Behaviour: Identical: each rewrite is the definition of the combinator.

